# Python
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Logs and stderr sinks. tier-poll.err is the cron stderr target for tier-poll.sh
# (`* * * * * .../tier-poll.sh 2>>.../tier-poll.err`), so it is a runtime artifact,
# not source. Empty is the healthy state.
*.log
*.err

# Secrets
.env

# Ad-hoc pre-edit copies. History belongs in git, not in .bak files.
# NOTE: sampler.py.bak (2026-06-12) does NOT match any committed version, so it is
# the only copy of that state - ignore it here, but do not delete it blindly.
*.bak

# Measurement data. The standing rule across this fleet is: scripts and write-ups go
# in git, a campaign's data does not. tier-trace.csv is live D4c tier telemetry,
# appended by cron every 60s since 2026-07-16 (~42k rows / 1.8 MB and growing).
# It is regenerable from tier-poll.sh, which SHOULD be committed.
*.csv
